	We also recall the main parameter sequences introduced in FLAG and which, for convenience, will be used often and systematically as follows:
   \begin{equation*}
    		\rho_{k} = \rho t_{k}^{p - 1} ,\; (\rho>0)\; \quad \text{and} \quad t_{k}^{p} - t_{k - 1}^{p} = t_{k}^{p - 1},\; (t_{-1} \equiv 0 \;\text{and}\; t_0 = 1),
	\end{equation*}	
	where $p = 1$ (if $\sigma = 0$) or $p = 2$ (if $\sigma > 0$), and $\tau_{k} = 1$ if $\sigma = 0$, or $\tau_{k} = t_{k}$ if $\sigma > 0$. We will also often use the following expression. For any $k\geq 0$ and any $\xi \in {\cal F}$ we define,

